abstract: >-
  A sixteen-prime-factor lower bound and exact completion criteria for
  Lehmer's totient problem. The full conjecture remains unproved.
  This revision proves that a quotient of at least 3 forces at least 20001
  prime factors and that no new solution of phi(n) | n+1 lies below 10^26,
  and removes every dependence on unrefereed work.

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23795673"
